course: dictionary
lesson: 6772
title: Oppose: against it, or on the other side
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To oppose something means to be against it and try to stop it. «Many British people at the time opposed the war» tells you they did not want the war and tried to stop it. Read the words around the word: a war, and people who felt it was wrong, give you the clue.
explain: Oppose can also mean to compete against someone, as in a game or an election. «The opposing team» is the team on the other side. Two sides, and one of them is the opposing side.
explain: Oppose is a verb, a doing word. It changes: oppose, opposes, opposed, opposing. Try your meaning in the sentence: «The court officials opposed the voyages» works if you put «were against» in the place of opposed.
fact: Oppose is a verb: oppose, opposes, opposed, opposing.
fact: «Oppose» means to be against something and try to stop it.
fact: «Oppose» can also mean to fight or compete against someone, like the opposing team in a game.
fact: «As opposed to» means in contrast with something, so you can compare two things.
fact: «Opposed» in the Ming story means that court officials were against the voyages.
exercise: «Many British people at the time opposed the war.» What does opposed mean here? | Went to see the war happen | Were unsure what the war was about | Cheered it on and joined in | *Were against it and wanted it stopped
exercise: «Our opposing team scored first in the match.» What does opposing mean? | Our own team in new shirts | The referee's helpers | *The team on the other side | The team that lost last year
exercise: The teacher opposed the two poems to compare them. What does opposed mean here? | Read them out loud | *Set them against each other to compare | Copied them neatly | Lost them both
test: Ella's dad strongly opposes the new road, so he wrote a letter. What does opposes mean? | Has never heard of the road | *Is against it and wants to stop it | Likes it very much | Is building the road
test: Which form of oppose is the past tense? | *opposed | oppose | opposes | opposing
exam: Which word best replaces oppose in «Many people opposed the plan»? | were happy with | were writing about | *were against | were rich in
